# Tutorial 04 — Images and Backgrounds
# @background declarations, [bg] switching, and scene composition.

@scenario {{SCENARIO_PREFIX}}_tutorial_04_images
@include {{CHARACTERS_INCLUDE}}
{{BG_DECL}}@label start
[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[set ui.textBoxAsset none]
[set ui.continueIndicator spinning_arrow]
[if tutorial_still]
[set ui.reduceMotion true]
[else]
[set ui.reduceMotion false]
[endif]
[if !tutorial_initialized]
[set tutorial_count 0]
[flag tutorial_initialized]
[endif]
[set ui.characterHeightFactor 1.5]
[set ui.characterBaselineY 1.5]
[set character.lavender.imageEffect none]
{{BG_START}}
[textspeed 28]
[autodelay 1650]
[show lavender center happy]
[wait 200]
Lavender: The background you see behind me was set with a single command before this scene started.
[show lavender center talking]
Lavender: This tutorial covers declaring backgrounds, switching them, and composing full scenes.

@label lesson_menu
[show lavender far_left talking]
> @background — declaring backgrounds -> section_declare
> [bg] — switching mid-scene -> section_switching
> Scene composition — background + characters -> section_composing
> Asset folders and naming -> section_organization
> Quick reference: background workflow -> quick_reference
> Practice: build a scene from scratch -> practice_scene
> Back to Tutorial Hub -> return_hub

# ─── Quick Reference ─────────────────────────────────────────────

@label quick_reference
[show lavender center talking]
Lavender: Backgrounds are declared once, then switched by ID:
narrator: {color=#8888cc}@background field_day assets/backgrounds/field_day.png{/color}
narrator: {color=#8888cc}[bg field_day]{/color}
narrator: {color=#8888cc}[transition fade 500]{/color}
narrator: {color=#8888cc}[bg cafe_night]{/color}
narrator: {color=#8888cc}[transition crossfade 700 field_evening]{/color}
[show lavender center happy]
Lavender: Checklist: clear IDs, correct asset paths, target-resolution images, and a transition only when the cut should feel smooth.
> Start the lesson sections -> section_declare
> Back to menu -> lesson_menu

# ─── @background ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

@label section_declare
[show lavender left talking]
Lavender: {b}@background{/b} registers an image file with an ID you'll use in scripts:
narrator: {color=#8888cc}@background field_day assets/backgrounds/field_day.png{/color}
narrator: {color=#8888cc}@background cafe_night assets/backgrounds/cafe_night.png{/color}
narrator: {color=#8888cc}@background classroom assets/backgrounds/school_classroom.png{/color}
[show lavender center talking]
Lavender: Structure: {b}@background{/b} {i}id{/i} {i}filepath{/i}
narrator: The {b}id{/b} is what you type in [bg] commands. The {b}filepath{/b} points to the image.
Lavender: Place declarations at the top of a script file, or in a shared definitions file.
narrator: {b}Naming convention:{/b} use {b}location_time{/b} — cafe_night, park_sunset, school_morning.
[show lavender center happy]
Lavender: Supported formats: PNG, JPG, WebP. Use images at your target resolution for best quality.
> Next: switching backgrounds -> section_switching
> Back to menu -> lesson_menu

# ─── [bg] ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@label section_switching
[show lavender right talking]
Lavender: {b}[bg]{/b} swaps the current background immediately:
narrator: {color=#8888cc}[bg field_day]{/color}
narrator: The old background vanishes. The new one appears on the same frame.
[show lavender center talking]
Lavender: For a smoother transition, put a {b}[transition]{/b} before the [bg]:
narrator: {color=#8888cc}[transition fade 500]{/color}
narrator: {color=#8888cc}[bg cafe_night]{/color}
narrator: The screen fades to black over 500ms, then the new background appears.
Lavender: Or crossfade directly between two backgrounds:
narrator: {color=#8888cc}[transition crossfade 700 cafe_night]{/color}
narrator: The old image dissolves into the new one over 700ms. No black screen.
[show lavender center happy]
Lavender: Tutorial 05 covers transitions in detail. For now: [transition] before [bg] = smooth; [bg] alone = instant cut.
> Next: scene composition -> section_composing
> Back to menu -> lesson_menu

# ─── Scene Composition ───────────────────────────────────────────

@label section_composing
[show lavender center talking]
Lavender: A complete scene beat is three steps: set background, place characters, write dialogue.
narrator: Here's the script for a minimal scene:
narrator: {color=#8888cc}[bg field_day]{/color}
narrator: {color=#8888cc}[show lavender center happy]{/color}
narrator: {color=#8888cc}Lavender: What a beautiful morning!{/color}
[show lavender left talking]
Lavender: Add a second character for a conversation:
narrator: {color=#8888cc}[bg cafe_night]{/color}
narrator: {color=#8888cc}[show lavender left talking]{/color}
narrator: {color=#8888cc}[show alex right happy]{/color}
narrator: {color=#8888cc}Lavender: You made it! I was starting to worry.{/color}
narrator: {color=#8888cc}Alex: Sorry — trains were a mess tonight.{/color}
[show lavender center talking]
Lavender: Background = stage. Characters = actors. Dialogue = performance. Change any one and the scene reads differently.
[show lavender center happy]
Lavender: The same dialogue in a cafe_night vs hospital_corridor creates an entirely different story.
> Next: asset organization -> section_organization
> Back to menu -> lesson_menu

# ─── Asset Organization ──────────────────────────────────────────

@label section_organization
[show lavender left talking]
Lavender: Folder structure that scales:
narrator: {b}assets/backgrounds/{/b} — all scene backgrounds.
narrator: {b}assets/characters/sprites/{/b} — character art. One subfolder per character if using layers.
narrator: {b}assets/cg/{/b} — full-screen CG illustrations.
narrator: {b}assets/ui/{/b} — text box frames, buttons, icons.
narrator: {b}assets/effects/{/b} — overlays, particles, weather.
[show lavender center talking]
Lavender: File naming rules:
narrator: {b}Do:{/b} cafe_night.png, school_hallway_rain.png, lavender_happy.png
narrator: {b}Don't:{/b} IMG_3847.png, bg2_final_v3.png, untitled.jpg
Lavender: When you have 50+ backgrounds, clear names are the difference between finding a file in 5 seconds and searching for 5 minutes.
[show lavender center happy]
Lavender: The engine resolves paths from your @background declarations. Folder depth doesn't matter — only the path does.
> Practice: build a scene -> practice_scene
> Back to menu -> lesson_menu

# ─── Practice ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@label practice_scene
[show lavender center talking]
Lavender: I'll walk you through building a scene step by step — the exact sequence you'd write in a real script.
[wait 300]
narrator: {b}Step 1:{/b} Declare the background.
narrator: {color=#8888cc}@background park_morning assets/backgrounds/park_morning.png{/color}
narrator: This goes at the top of your file, before any labels.
[wait 200]
narrator: {b}Step 2:{/b} Set the background.
narrator: {color=#8888cc}[bg park_morning]{/color}
narrator: Now the player sees the park.
[wait 200]
narrator: {b}Step 3:{/b} Place the character.
narrator: {color=#8888cc}[show lavender center happy]{/color}
narrator: Lavender appears at center with a happy expression.
[wait 200]
narrator: {b}Step 4:{/b} Write dialogue.
narrator: {color=#8888cc}Lavender: The cherry blossoms are incredible this year.{/color}
narrator: {color=#8888cc}narrator: Petals drifted across the path like pink snow.{/color}
[wait 200]
narrator: {b}Step 5:{/b} Change location.
narrator: {color=#8888cc}[transition fade 500]{/color}
narrator: {color=#8888cc}[bg cafe_night]{/color}
narrator: {color=#8888cc}[show lavender left talking]{/color}
narrator: {color=#8888cc}Lavender: Let's grab coffee. My treat.{/color}
[show lavender center happy]
Lavender: That's the full pattern: declare, set, show, speak, transition, repeat.
Lavender: Try it now — add a new @background declaration at the top of this file, then insert a [bg] command anywhere in the practice section.
> Back to menu -> lesson_menu

